        "date_dead_since": null,
        "date_published": "2026-08-06T11:28:00+00:00",
        "description": "<p>This started life as a graphics tool for a specific problem: gen AI can make retro-styled sprites but can't follow exact hardware constraints of pixels and colors.<p>While building this I liked the idea that I can fan-out to any retro videogame console or handheld's specifications.<p>I then devised my own declarative language - Demotic - to express the game you want to build as concisely and naturally as possible without implementation detail. To work on different machines, you use relative units, like vw, vh, vmin, vmax.<p>It has a web UI, CLI and NPM package. Still a work in progress.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49195251\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49195251</a></p>\n<p>Points: 15</p>\n<p># Comments: 1</p>",
